@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Remote Filesystem over SSH
  "SSH-backed RemoteFS with safe Mason symlink writes and collision detection."

  Provides:
    - remote.RemoteFS @source("symbol:RemoteFS")
    - remote.FileMode @source("symbol:FileMode")
    - remote.EntryKind @source("symbol:EntryKind")
    - remote.RemoteEntry @source("symbol:RemoteEntry")
    - remote.SymlinkRequest @source("symbol:SymlinkRequest")
    - remote.PathCollisionError @source("symbol:PathCollisionError")
    - remote.SSHFS @source("symbol:SSHFS")
    - remote.NewSSHFS @source("symbol:NewSSHFS")
    - remote.CheckSafeSymlink @source("symbol:CheckSafeSymlink")
    - remote.EnsureSafeSymlink @source("symbol:EnsureSafeSymlink")
    - remote.RemotePath @source("symbol:RemotePath")

  Consumes:
    - remote.CommandRunner
    - domain.BlobHex
    - domain.BlobHashPrefix

  Invariants:
    - Mason MUST NOT overwrite non-symlink paths or user-owned symlinks not targeting objects/
    - Missing symlink paths MUST be allowed before write
    - RemotePath MUST join the store root with site-relative paths using forward slashes

  OutOfScope:
    - Manifest read/write (owned by the manifest store)
    - Blob byte transfer (owned by rsync)

  Scenario (happy-path): Create managed symlink
    Given a missing link path and a target under objects/
    When EnsureSafeSymlink runs
    Then the symlink is created via SSH

  Scenario (negative): Path collision
    Given an existing file or non-Mason symlink at the link path
    When CheckSafeSymlink runs
    Then it returns PathCollisionError
